{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nEpic `inferior-seaborgium-aruanas` makes release a first-class rebar ticket field synced both ways with Jira's `fixVersions`. Its approach step 1 requires an ADR before any code, so the later children (reducer, inbound, outbound, missing-version alert, surfaces) build against one recorded design. The operator settled the product decisions on 2026-11-05 (epic description and comments). This ADR records them and settles what the epic delegates to it: the replayed event carrier, the field name, the `FIELD_CONTRACT` class, name identity and renames, and archived/deleted versions.\n\n## Approach\n\nWrite `docs/adr/0123-jira-fix-versions-release-field.md` (next free number: the last marker is `docs/adr/.numbers/0122`, and no open Gerrit change exists on 2026-11-09) with a `## Decision` section of numbered items:\n\n1. **Field shape.** Compiled state gains `releases`: a list of Jira version names, default `[]`, insertion-ordered, no duplicates. Names only: no release records, status or dates.\n2. **Carrier.** A new event `RELEASE_DELTA {\"added\", \"removed\", \"source\"?}` folded by `process_release_delta` with `process_tag_delta`'s rules (`src/rebar/reducer/_processors.py:429-449`): removals first, then additions. Rejected: a field selector on `TAG_DELTA`, because an older clone that knows `TAG_DELTA` would fold release names into `tags`; a new type takes the preserve-and-ignore path for unknown types (`src/rebar/reducer/_version.py:8-16`). `SCHEMA_VERSION` 5 → 6, readers before writers (reconcile host first), as `docs/event-schema.md` prescribes for a new body type.\n3. **Symmetry.** `FIELD_CONTRACT[\"releases\"]`: `ADD_WINS`, conflict class `set`, `outbound_name=\"fixVersions\"`, like `labels` (`src/rebar/reconciler/_field_contract.py:108-119`); `conflict_resolver.FIELD_CLASSES[\"releases\"] = \"set\"`.\n4. **Inbound.** Set-diff Jira `fixVersions[].name` against `releases` like `_diff_labels_inbound` (`src/rebar/reconciler/inbound_collection_diffs.py:194-214`); write `RELEASE_DELTA` with `source=\"inbound\"`, suppressing no-ops and skipping the write when the reducer fails, like `_inbound_update_apply_labels` (`src/rebar/reconciler/apply_inbound_events.py:322-389`). An unobserved `fixVersions` key yields no diff.\n5. **Outbound.** ADD names the issue lacks; REMOVE only names in the local ever-seen intent set (non-inbound `RELEASE_DELTA.added` and `SNAPSHOT` releases), mirroring the intent gate in `src/rebar/reconciler/outbound_labels.py:43-85`. Per-item verbs only: Cloud `PUT /rest/api/3/issue/{key}` with `{\"update\":{\"fixVersions\":[{\"add\":{\"name\":N}}]}}` or `remove`; Data Center `issue.update(update={\"fixVersions\":[...]})`, the verb the DC label remove uses (`src/rebar/reconciler/adapters/jira_datacenter/_issues.py:196`). Never `set`.\n6. **Same pass.** Outbound wins through the existing suppression in `src/rebar/reconciler/inbound_differ.py:298-322`, extended to releases.\n7. **Identity and renames.** The name is the identity (Jira Cloud OpenAPI `Version.name`: unique per project). A rename of a Jira-originated release surfaces as remove old plus add new. A rebar-set name that a rename or deletion makes stop existing follows item 8: it stays with an alert, and after a rename the new name also arrives inbound, because the withheld outbound ADD suppresses the inbound REMOVE under item 6. Recorded as a consequence.\n8. **Missing version.** Read each bound project's versions once per pass (Cloud `GET /rest/api/3/project/{key}/versions`; DC `project_versions`). Withhold an ADD the project lacks, keep the name, write one `BRIDGE_ALERT` per (ticket, name) with reason `release-version-missing:<name>`, retry every pass, and resolve the alert when the name is no longer withheld. An unreadable version list means unknown: no alert, no resolution. The bridge never creates versions.\n9. **Archived and deleted.** Withhold an archived version like a missing one (reason `release-version-archived:<name>`): Jira's behavior on adding one is unverified (no version exists on the site, and the Atlassian pages checked on 2026-11-09 do not state it), and withholding cannot write an unexpected value. Archived names on an issue still sync inbound; their REMOVE is attempted. A deleted version is absent, so item 8 applies; when Jira strips it from issues, inbound removes it.\n10. **Out of scope.** Affects versions (`versions`); parent inheritance (`list --release X` returns exactly tickets whose own `releases` hold X); any config key.\n11. **Surfaces.** `rebar edit --add-release/--remove-release/--set-releases` (set is an add-wins delta like `--set-tags`), `rebar list --release`, `rebar show`, library `edit_ticket` keywords `add_releases`/`remove_releases`/`set_releases` and `list_tickets(release=)`, and the derived MCP parameters and read `outputSchema`s.\n\nAn `## Evidence` section records the read-only Jira checks of 2026-11-09 (PST), each with its endpoint: the `fixVersions` field schema (`/rest/api/3/field`); REB-7015 editmeta without `fixVersions`; 0 versions in all 144 visible projects and 0 issues matching `fixVersion is not EMPTY`; Atlassian's documented Set/Add/Remove support for Fix Versions; and the edit endpoint's statement that it \"doesn't check screen configurations\", which contradicts the epic's REB edit-screen prerequisite and is left for the production-verification child to settle live.\n\nThen add the ADR to the Reconciler list in `docs/adr/README.md` after 0121, and create `docs/adr/.numbers/0123` holding the ADR filename.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `docs/adr/0123-jira-fix-versions-release-field.md` (new)\n- `docs/adr/.numbers/0123` (new marker)\n- `docs/adr/README.md` (index entry)\n\nDocumentation only: no code, no new testable behavior.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] `docs/adr/0123-jira-fix-versions-release-field.md` has `**Status:** Accepted` and a `## Decision` section with one numbered item for each of the 11 Approach points.\n- [ ] Decision item 2 names the rejected `TAG_DELTA` field selector with its older-clone corruption reason.\n- [ ] Decision item 2 records `SCHEMA_VERSION` 6 with readers-before-writers rollout.\n- [ ] The `## Evidence` section lists the 5 read-only findings, each with its endpoint or source.\n- [ ] The `## Evidence` section names the edit-screen contradiction.\n- [ ] `python scripts/check_adr_numbers.py` exits 0 with `docs/adr/.numbers/0123` present.\n- [ ] `docs/adr/README.md` links `0123-jira-fix-versions-release-field.md`.\n- [ ] `env -u JIRA_URL -u JIRA_USER -u JIRA_API_TOKEN make verify` exits 0 on the commit pushed for review."}},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1794257833465275001,"uuid":"52e245cd-a050-4df6-8fbd-d68b87fb7496"}